+
+Backfill behaviour
+------------------
+* start_date = 2026-09-01: the earliest date we have raw data for.  Airflow
+  will never schedule runs before this date, so there is no risk of loading
+  non-existent files.
+* catchup = True: when the DAG is unpaused, the scheduler creates one run for
+  every day from 2026-09-01 up to today and queues them automatically.
+* max_active_runs = 1: DuckDB allows only one writer at a time.  Serial
+  execution prevents the lock-file errors that would occur if two daily runs
+  tried to write web.duckdb simultaneously.
+
+Idempotency
+-----------
+Each run operates on exactly one day determined by the DAG's logical_date
+(the start of the data interval Airflow assigned to that run).  The task
+deletes any existing rows for that date before inserting, so re-running a
+day is always safe and will never double-count.
 """
 
